{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>That has legs.</b> I have already elaborated in my work on Tur Yoreh De'ah (siman 85) that the essence follows Rashi's explanation here, that it must have long legs near its neck. And those who err to permit it because no such species exists — I answered them that indeed only one species is found among the four that are eight, which HaShem listed in tractate Tehorot (Ḥullin 65a); and likewise the impure species that lack legs in this manner are not found before us, and they are the majority, as was stated earlier (Ḥullin 63a) — for Scripture enumerates only the few, and here it enumerates the pure ones; if so, the impure ones are the majority. From this point on there is no proof from the fact that this species is not found to say that it does not exist in the world, since there are certainly many species that are not found at all in our locale. Therefore every God-fearer and trembler should fear and dread lest he stretch out his hand to this abomination, and should rebuke those who send forth their hand. And behold, from the day my words were heard in the Maghreb and the many separated themselves from them, HaShem has not again struck with this plague, and they have not been seen for more than twelve years — for Torah and good deeds are a shield against punishment."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "The phrase 'ששהם שמנה' (literally 'that they are eight') refers to the eight names of four kosher locust species listed by mnemonic in the Mishnah; left hyper-literal. 'במערב' rendered as 'in the Maghreb,' the author's native region."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:55:21.573871736Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}